A||||4||Two88GTs||How do you guys change your headlights?||||1||
Z||000000||Two88GTs||09-29-2001||09:39 PM||||I just looked at the DIY manual and the Haynes manual for changing a headlight, and their procedures seem needlessly long.  All I do is remove the plastic headlight housing underneath the hood(4 T-15 screws), remove plug from dead bulb, undo the two Philips screws from the top chrome trim ring, pull the trim ring towards you, and the headlight should fall right out.  No need to pull the headlight spring or reaim the headlight.  <BR>Anybody else agree?||||reg||1
Z||000001||recluse||09-29-2001||11:24 PM||||Just replaced one today. Did it exactly how you explained.  I lost my haynes manual.... never was much help anyways!  ||||reg||14
Z||000002||MontanaFiero||09-30-2001||01:42 AM||||I converted to H-4 halogen. Hopefully I will never have to do it the "hard" way again...<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||maryjane||09-30-2001||01:53 AM||||Your right, the Haynes manual goes the long way around. Somtimes I think I've picked up a manual that has the wrong cover on it or something. Doesn't seem like they are talking about a Fiero at all. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
